  "name": "US Brokerage Account Statement",
  "emoji": "📈",
  "description": "US individual brokerage account statement (Schwab, Fidelity, Vanguard, Merrill, Morgan Stanley, IBKR and similar). Removes only client-identifying data: account holder, joint holder, trustee and beneficiary names (capitals on registration lines and address blocks, or normal case after a label), account numbers in labeled, dashed, Fidelity/IBKR, partial and masked forms, SSN / tax ID (also masked), client phone numbers, the city, state and ZIP line, plus mailing addresses and e-mails from the built-in detectors. The generic name and account-number detectors are off on purpose, so security names and CUSIPs are never taken for people or accounts. Keeps account types (INDIVIDUAL TOD, ROTH IRA), security names, tickers, CUSIPs, quantities, prices, values, balances, income, fees, cost basis, gains/losses, dates, custodian names, toll-free service numbers and the advisor's name. Limits: the custodian's own street address and ZIP look like the client's and are covered too (remove them with the X), an unlabeled normal-case name without a middle initial is not detected, and signatures and QR codes need a manual box.",
